Subject: [PATCH 1/2] hw/ia64: wire configured ISA parallel ports

Instantiate current ISA parallel devices on the PIIX4-owned ISA bus, route IRQ7 through the architectural I/O SAPIC path, exercise LPT1 through the sparse legacy-I/O window, and document the resulting compatibility topology.

diff --git a/configs/devices/ia64-softmmu/default.mak b/configs/devices/ia64-softmmu/default.mak
index bd6e038..062da05 100644
--- a/configs/devices/ia64-softmmu/default.mak
+++ b/configs/devices/ia64-softmmu/default.mak
@@ -13,3 +13,6 @@ CONFIG_PCKBD=y
 
 # Standard ISA floppy controller; PIIX supplies its IRQ and i8257 DMA paths.
 CONFIG_FDC_ISA=y
+
+# Legacy printer ports use the same PIIX ISA-to-I/O-SAPIC routing.
+CONFIG_PARALLEL=y
